# rtech-agents deploy environment for the k-board LXC (your deploy host).
# Copy to ~/rtech-agents/.env and fill in. NEVER commit a filled .env.
# Secret VALUES come from Vaultwarden at install time; only *_ref notes live here.
#
# The units do NOT read ANTHROPIC_* from here. The systemd user units scrub the
# ~/.cc-env poison (ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL/API_KEY/MODEL/DEFAULT_*_MODEL) via an
# `env -u` wrapper so the real engine uses the box's subscription CLI auth with
# its own model defaults. Do NOT add ANTHROPIC_* here.

# --- NATS (fleet bus) --------------------------------------------------------
# The live fleet NATS server all three roles share.
NATS_URL=nats://127.0.0.1:4222

# --- web-chat edge -----------------------------------------------------------
# Bind the edge to the k-board LXC's LAN address ONLY. NOT 0.0.0.0, NOT public.
# dev_stack used DEV_STACK_PORT; the deployed edge reads RTECH_WEBCHAT_PORT /
# RTECH_WEBCHAT_HOST (rtech_webchat.config.WebchatConfig.from_env).
RTECH_WEBCHAT_HOST=127.0.0.1
RTECH_WEBCHAT_PORT=3800
RTECH_WEBCHAT_NATS_URL=nats://127.0.0.1:4222

# --- agentd / orchestrator ---------------------------------------------------
# agentd identity comes from the systemd instance name: rtech-agentd@<id> sets
# RTECH_AGENT_ID=%i. DO NOT set RTECH_AGENT_ID in this file — EnvironmentFile
# values reach the process and OVERRIDE the unit's %i, silently collapsing every
# instance on the host to one shared identity (all three trio agentds consumed
# agentd-birk's lane until this line was removed from a live deploy). Set it
# here ONLY for a deliberate single-unit, single-identity box.
# RTECH_AGENT_ID=agentd-birk
# RTECH_TARGET_AGENT_ID is the orchestrator's routing target; RTECH_SINGLE_AGENT_ID
# is accepted as a back-compat alias. The orchestrator FAILS LOUDLY at startup if
# neither (nor a registry) is set — it never falls back to a shared literal.
RTECH_TARGET_AGENT_ID=agentd-birk

# --- edge API key ------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional shared key the edge checks on task/steer ingress (rtech_webchat reads
# RTECH_AGENTS_API_KEY). REF ONLY: the real value is fetched from Vaultwarden at
# install and written into ~/rtech-agents/.env by the operator, NEVER here.
# Vaultwarden ref: <your-secret-store-path>/RTECH_AGENTS_API_KEY
# RTECH_AGENTS_API_KEY=

# --- bounded restart + context rotation --------------------------
# The supervisor bounds BOTH its own restart loop and session context growth.
# All values are optional; the shipped defaults are shown. Do NOT set these to
# fight systemd — the in-process restart budget bounds ONE unit lifetime, and
# systemd's Restart=on-failure (below) is the OUTER loop. When the restart
# circuit opens (budget spent) agentd exits non-zero on purpose, and systemd
# relaunches the unit with a fresh budget.
#
# Restart circuit breaker: capped attempts, exponential backoff, healthy reset.
# RTECH_RESTART_MAX_ATTEMPTS=5
# RTECH_RESTART_BACKOFF_BASE_S=1
# RTECH_RESTART_BACKOFF_CAP_S=60
# RTECH_RESTART_HEALTHY_RESET_S=300
#
# Context rotation: summarize + swap to a fresh session at a turn/age bound so the
# transcript never grows unbounded. The summary turn is a SINGLE bounded attempt.
# RTECH_ROTATE_MAX_TURNS=200
# RTECH_ROTATE_MAX_AGE_S=86400
# RTECH_ROTATE_SUMMARY_TIMEOUT_S=120

# --- engine mode -------------------------------------------------------------
# The real Claude engine (DEFAULT) needs an authenticated `claude` CLI on PATH
# for the target user (birk): subscription auth, NOT an API key. The operator logs in
# ONCE as birk (`claude` -> browser login) before enabling agentd. The units
# scrub ANTHROPIC_* so the CLI's own subscription auth + defaults are used.
# Leaving DEV_STACK_ENGINE unset (as shipped) selects the real Claude engine.
# For an offline bus-wiring smoke test WITHOUT a real model, set:
#   DEV_STACK_ENGINE=scripted
# (Commented out -- real engine is the deployed default.)
# DEV_STACK_ENGINE=scripted

# --- chatd Discord edge (opt-in) ---------------------------------------------
# The product's primary chat surface: a DUMB edge that mints a typed TaskFrame
# from each gated Discord message and renders agent turns back (attributed). It
# fail-closes without a token, inbox, AND stack id, so install.sh copies its unit
# but does NOT enable it — the operator opts in (see README "chatd Discord edge").
#
# REQUIRED: the shared stack stamp. Every TaskFrame this edge (and
# the web-chat edge) publishes is stamped with it; the orchestrator only consumes
# matching tasks. There is NO default — a shared literal is fail-open producer
# addressing. This var was previously MISSING from this file; set it once here.
RTECH_STACK_ID=dev
# NATS URL for chatd (defaults to the live fleet bus if unset).
RTECH_CHATD_NATS_URL=nats://127.0.0.1:4222
# REQUIRED: the designated free-response inbox channel id. This is the ONLY
# channel where chatd answers without an @mention ("treat Discord as leaked").
RTECH_CHATD_INBOX_CHANNEL=
# Bot-token indirection REF only (env:<ENV_VAR>). NEVER a literal token.
RTECH_CHATD_TOKEN_REF=env:RTECH_CHATD_BOT_TOKEN
# The token VALUE is fetched from Vaultwarden at install and written here by the
# operator, NEVER committed. Vaultwarden ref: <your-secret-store-path>/RTECH_CHATD_BOT_TOKEN
# RTECH_CHATD_BOT_TOKEN=
# Comma-separated agent ids the task fans out to; the COUNT derives scope
# (1=single, 2=duo, 3=trio). Empty = a single-scope task routed to the
# orchestrator's configured default target.
RTECH_CHATD_PARTICIPANTS=
# Bot-author policy: none | mentions. `all` is REJECTED fail-closed (security
# floor). Defaults to none when unset.
# RTECH_CHATD_ALLOW_BOTS=mentions

# --- Telegram long-poll edge, opt-in -----------------------
# rtech-tgd reuses RTECH_CHATD_TOKEN_REF for its polling identity. It and every
# RTECH_TG_IDENTITY_MAP value must be env:<ENV_VAR> references; secret values
# are retrieved by the operator from Vaultwarden into those env vars and are
# never committed.
# RTECH_TG_ALLOWED_GROUPS=-1001234567890
# RTECH_TG_IDENTITY_MAP=agentd-nimbus=env:RTECH_TG_TOKEN_NIMBUS,agentd-birk=env:RTECH_TG_TOKEN_BIRK,agentd-sprocket=env:RTECH_TG_TOKEN_SPROCKET
# RTECH_TG_TOKEN_NIMBUS=
# RTECH_TG_TOKEN_BIRK=
# RTECH_TG_TOKEN_SPROCKET=
# RTECH_TG_POLL_TIMEOUT_S=30
# Long polling opens no inbound port and requires no webhook or public domain.

# --- intake / trio debate, opt-in --------------
# NOTE: RTECH_CHATD_PARTICIPANTS above is chatd's own outbound task mint —
# DISTINCT from the intake debate roster below.
# Deterministic channel intake: unset/0 = intake off, byte-identical legacy
# behavior. See deploy/kboard/watcher-canary.md for the full trio recipe.
# RTECH_CHATD_INTAKE_ENABLED=1
# Intake scope: listed (allow-list + free-response channels) | all-channels.
# RTECH_CHATD_INTAKE_MODE=listed
# Mention-id and name/prefix triggers for the intake hit-gate.
# RTECH_CHATD_INTAKE_MEMBER_IDS=
# RTECH_CHATD_INTAKE_NAME_TRIGGERS=nimbus,birk,sprocket
# RTECH_CHATD_INTAKE_TRIGGER_PREFIXES=
# REQUIRED when intake is enabled (no default; agentd-<name> id-space).
# RTECH_CHATD_TRIAGE_AGENT=agentd-nimbus
# Optional trio/duo debate roster: a hit mints ONE multi-participant TaskFrame
# (orchestrator fans out). agentd-<name> convention enforced; triage agent must
# be a member. Unset = single-scope intake exactly as before.
# RTECH_CHATD_DEBATE_PARTICIPANTS=agentd-nimbus,agentd-birk,agentd-sprocket
# Optional per-agent home channel id for cron/cross-platform delivery.
# DISCORD_HOME_CHANNEL=

# --- wake (triage) capability, opt-in ----------------------------
# Setting RTECH_WAKE_ALLOWED_AGENTS IS the opt-in that THIS agentd becomes a
# WAKER: it may mint a wake TaskFrame toward a teammate. ONLY the triage deploy
# (Nimbus) should set it. A woken agent must NOT be a waker — leaving this unset
# (the default) is what bounds wake-chaining (a woken agent with no allow-list
# cannot wake anyone). The value is a comma list of ``agentd-<name>`` ids this
# agent may wake (e.g. agentd-birk,agentd-sprocket). REQUIRES RTECH_STACK_ID (a
# minted wake frame must be stack-scoped); a blank stack fails closed at startup.
# Left UNSET here so a default agentd is not a waker.
# RTECH_WAKE_ALLOWED_AGENTS=agentd-birk,agentd-sprocket
